1305: #  store_Nbit_word helpers and do reach the arms.  So the operator path for BYTES is not a
1306: #  path at all, and the row was vacuous by construction -- the CHANNEL rule's own failure,
1307: #  caught by the table.  Guest `st.b' is legal at every offset (byte accesses skip the m88k
1308: #  alignment check; `rb mask' stores a byte at 0x3f this way), so the accept side is pinned
