1: #!/usr/bin/env python3
2: """#500 sgideprimop DETECTOR -- draw_primitive()'s unimplemented drawing op.
3: 
4: WHAT THE FIX DID.  `draw_primitive()' ended with
5: 
6:     default: fatal("[ sgi_de: UNIMPLEMENTED drawing op = 0x%08x, ... ]"); exit(1);
7: 
8: and `op' comes straight from a guest-written register.  The switch discriminates
9: on the TOP BYTE only, so the domain is 256 values and only two are implemented.
10: A guest-written drawing op ended the host process.  It is now a latched decline
11: that falls out of the switch and returns.
12: 
13: *** THE TWO KILLERS THAT MATTER ARE NOT EXOTIC VALUES.  crmfbreg.h names four
14: primitives, and note the constants are FULL 32-BIT VALUES, not top-byte indices:
15: DE_PRIM_POINT 0x00000000, LINE 0x01000000, TRIANGLE 0x02000000, RECTANGLE
16: 0x03000000.  Writing them as "0x01" invites a `case 0x02:' that can NEVER match,
17: because the switch compares `op & 0xff000000'.  The model implements LINE and
18: RECTANGLE only.  POINT and TRIANGLE are DOCUMENTED
19: primitives interleaved with the implemented pair.  And POINT is 0x00000000,
20: which is ALSO THE RESET VALUE: dev_sgi_re_init memsets the device struct, so
21: CRIME_DE_PRIMITIVE reads 0 until a guest writes it.  A guest that set the START
22: bit having never written the primitive register at all died here.  It need not
23: choose a bad value; it need only omit a good one. ***
24: 
25: CONTRACT (vacuity-floor clause (e)) -- which edits this detector is designed to
26: catch, and which it is NOT:
27: 
28:   CATCHES
29:     * reinstatement of the host kill, at either killer value (`pt surv',
30:       `tri surv') and at the reset path (`reset surv');
31:     * *** THE KILL REINSTATED AS exit(0) RATHER THAN exit(1). ***  This is the
32:       one that matters most here and it is why no row in this file uses exit
33:       status as its only oracle.  EXIT STATUS CANNOT VARY between "declined and
34:       then quit" and "died with status 0" -- a sibling round MEASURED that shape
35:       as a 48/48 clean sweep on the day this was written.  Every survival row is
36:       PAIRED with a positive post-draw observable (`* live'), which reads
37:       "absent" when the host is gone and therefore reds on a death HOWEVER THE
38:       DEATH IS SPELLED;
39:     * loss of the latch in EITHER direction, and they are different mutants:
40:         - dropping the `!' makes the bit never set, so the announce NEVER fires
41:           -- a SILENT decline, caught by the `* decl' rows wanting one message;
42:         - dropping the `|=' makes the announce fire EVERY time -- a FLOOD, which
43:           a "at least one message" row PASSES.  Only `two once' catches it,
44:           because it performs TWO distinct defaulted draws in ONE session and
45:           wants EXACTLY one message.
46:       *** THE FLOOD MUTANT IS THE ONE THAT ESCAPES A NAIVE ROW SET, and this
47:       file's own author had it backwards in a pass-2 brief until the glm seat
48:       corrected him. ***
49:     * *** ANY WIDENING OF THE SWITCH MASK INTO THE LIVE MODIFIER BITS.  This took
50:       THREE passes and the first two repairs were both cell-shaped: `& 0xffff0000'
51:       swept the 19-row version clean, so two rows were added carrying bits 16 and
52:       18 -- and then `& 0xff020000' swept the 21-row version clean, because bit 17
53:       was still unpinned.  The rows now carry ALL THREE live modifier bits
54:       (RL 16, TB 17, SKIP_END 18, derived by grepping every read of `op'), so the
55:       WIDENING half of the class is closed rather than sampled. ***
56:     * *** AND A NARROWED SWITCH MASK AT ANY OF THE SIX HIGH BITS.  The first
57:       attempt pinned bit 26 ALONE and a seat swept it with a bit-27 narrowing;
58:       the space is bits 26-31, which must be zero for an implemented op, so all
59:       six are now enumerated (`dec b26'..`dec b31').  ***
60:     * *** the older, narrower form of that clause, kept for its reasoning:
61:       The implemented values are 0x01 and 0x03, so only bits 24-25 carry
